CAT = "phrebEthics"; SEG = "ETH"
Q = [
("A broker learns that the lot she is listing sits on a road right-of-way reserved by the city. Under her duty of honesty she should:",
 "Disclose it to buyers", ["Wait until a buyer asks", "Mention it after the sale", "Raise the price to cover it"],
 "Practitioners must not conceal or misrepresent material facts about a property. A reserved right-of-way affects value and use, so buyers must be told before they commit."),
("A broker's spouse wants to buy a house the broker has listed for a client. The broker should first:",
 "Tell the seller in writing", ["Lower the asking price", "Keep it confidential", "Ask a salesperson to handle it quietly"],
 "A broker must disclose any personal interest to the client. Article 1491 of the Civil Code bars an agent from buying, in person or through another, property entrusted to him for sale without the principal's consent."),
("A broker wants to post a lot that another broker holds under an exclusive authority to sell. She should first:",
 "Get the listing broker's consent", ["Post it with a lower price", "Call the owner directly", "Remove the owner's name"],
 "Advertising another practitioner's exclusive listing without consent undercuts that broker and confuses the owner. Cooperation goes through the listing broker."),
("Two brokers are working on the same listing. The proper way for them to share the commission is:",
 "By a written co-broker agreement", ["By who meets the buyer last", "Through the buyer's choice", "By equal shares, as fixed by R.A. 9646"],
 "Co-brokerage arrangements should be agreed in writing before the deal so that commission sharing is clear and disputes between practitioners are avoided."),
("A broker posts online that a competing broker is dishonest, with no basis. This conduct is:",
 "Unethical disparagement", ["Fair advertising", "Allowed if true in part", "A buyer's protection"],
 "An unfounded public accusation against a colleague is unprofessional conduct, a ground for suspension or revocation under Section 19(c) of R.A. 9646, and may also expose the broker to a defamation suit."),
("A client asks whether he should pay capital gains tax or creditable withholding tax on a sale. A broker who is unsure should:",
 "Refer him to a tax professional", ["Guess the likely tax", "Tell him the buyer always pays both taxes", "Let the buyer decide"],
 "Practitioners should not give advice beyond their competence. Tax questions belong to a tax practitioner or the BIR, and the broker should say so."),
("A broker receives an offer for a listed lot after the seller has already accepted another. The broker should:",
 "Still inform the seller", ["Discard the second offer", "Tell the buyer to bid more", "Keep it as a backup secretly"],
 "As agent, the broker acts for the seller and must keep the principal informed; under Article 1909 he answers for negligence. Whether a later offer matters is the seller's decision, not the broker's."),
("A broker advertises a subdivision lot as 'flood-free' though she has seen it under water. This is:",
 "Misrepresentation", ["Puffery that is allowed", "Fine if the price is low", "The developer's problem only"],
 "False statements of fact in advertising are misrepresentation, unlike harmless opinion. They can ground suspension or revocation under R.A. 9646 for unprofessional conduct."),
("A broker accepts a commission from both the seller and the buyer without telling either. This is wrong mainly because it:",
 "Hides a conflict of interest", ["Doubles the tax due", "Is allowed only for raw land and farm lots", "Breaks a zoning rule"],
 "Taking compensation from both sides without full disclosure and consent divides the broker's loyalty. Under Article 1891 of the Civil Code an agent must account to the principal for whatever he receives by virtue of the agency, and hidden double pay is unprofessional conduct under Section 19(c) of R.A. 9646."),
("A broker is offered a 'finder's fee' by a lender for steering clients to it. Before accepting, the broker must:",
 "Disclose it to the client", ["Hide it from the client", "Share it with the seller", "Split it with salespersons"],
 "Article 1891 of the Civil Code makes an agent account for and deliver whatever he receives by virtue of the agency, even if not owing to the principal, so a fee tied to the client's deal must be disclosed."),
("The Code of Ethics and Responsibilities for real estate service practitioners is adopted by:",
 "The Board of Real Estate Service", ["The Department of Trade and Industry", "The Supreme Court", "Each city council"],
 "Section 35 of R.A. 9646 has the Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service adopt and promulgate the Code of Ethics and Responsibilities, prepared by the accredited professional organization."),
("Unprofessional or unethical conduct by a licensed broker, after notice and hearing, may lead the Board to:",
 "Suspend or revoke the license", ["Raise the broker's taxes", "Cancel the titles of the client's properties", "Fine the buyer"],
 "Section 19 of R.A. 9646 lists unprofessional or unethical conduct, and violation of the Code of Ethics, among the grounds for suspension or revocation of a certificate of registration."),
]
